source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: carol's audience covers no file that exists, so there is nothing for the
card to open and the proof cannot run.

The card's identity and its recipient are written and are correct: the
enrollment is additive and complete except for the one claim it exists to
make. A canary encrypted for the occasion is deliberately not what runs
here — it would prove that a fresh file made from a fresh rule opens, which
is not the question.

Give carol a secret, then re-run this verb:

    safix set carol <name>
    safix enroll carol
